From 06e2d6b38b0c4a546920afadc3ee2a5a28446469 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rogerbacardit <rogerbacardit@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:16:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Track MIDI IN: a USB-A channel per track

A USB-A controller's every channel played the selected track, so a
sequencer sending several channels at once (a KeyStep Pro's four tracks)
collapsed onto one track. A track may now claim a channel (its MIDI IN,
SEL by default): that channel plays and records into that track whatever
is selected. Unclaimed channels still follow the selection, so a Set with
no claim behaves exactly as before.

- engine ext_route.rs: `extmap` is `<active>[;<ch>:<dest>]*`; the ledger
  is per channel (the same key on two channels is two notes); a wheel is
  recentred only on a chain no channel reaches any more.
- track/midi-in.ts: the per-track setting, carried in the UI blob; the
  lower track wins a channel two tracks claim, so the engine and the
  recording always agree.
- track menu (Shift + track): a MIDI IN row, jog to it, knob 1 turns it.
- Manual: playing.md "A channel for each track", controls.md.

Gate: local suites (logic incl. new midi-in.mjs, app-loop, screenshot with
the track menu baselines updated, perf, source-rules, host-globals,
typecheck) and cargo test (6 new ext_route tests). Device tier not run yet:
the box runs the v0.37.0 store build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
