diff --git a/site/manual/playing.md b/site/manual/playing.md
index 4c3dc7f0..a1d3058c 100644
--- a/site/manual/playing.md
+++ b/site/manual/playing.md
@@ -84,9 +84,28 @@ them, without touching the pattern.
 Plug a class-compliant USB MIDI keyboard or groovebox into the Move's **USB-A**
 port. It plays the **selected track**, just like the pads.
 
-- **Any MIDI channel** plays the selected track. Choose the destination on the Move.
+- **Any MIDI channel** plays the selected track. Choose the destination on the Move,
+  or give a track its own channel (below).
 - **Velocity** comes from the keyboard. Full velocity only affects the pads.
 - **Recording** works as with the pads: live, step recording, and hold-step + key.
 - On a **drum track**, C1 (MIDI note 36) plays pad 1, C#1 pad 2, and so on.
 - **Mod wheel** and **pitch bend** reach the synth live but are not recorded.
 - Other CCs, aftertouch and MIDI clock are ignored.
+
+### A channel for each track
+
+A controller that sends several channels at once, such as a sequencer with one
+track per channel, can play several Movy tracks together.
+
+1. Hold **Shift** and press the track's button. Its menu comes up.
+2. Turn the **jog** to **MIDI IN**.
+3. Turn **knob 1** to the channel, **CH 1** to **CH 16**. **Back** closes the menu.
+
+![MIDI IN in the track menu](../assets/screens/track_menu_midi_in.png){ .small }
+
+- That channel now plays that track, whichever track is selected, and records
+  into it.
+- Channels no track has claimed still play the selected track.
+- **SEL**, the default, gives the channel back to the selected track.
+- If two tracks take the same channel, the lower-numbered one plays it.
+- Each Set remembers its tracks' channels.
